calibration = (3137556 - 1568788) / 4096 = 383 instructions per blst_fp_mul (the published value; binary hash as published).
price = (7560540 - 3780240) / 4096 = 922.925 instructions per lane (mean over the harness lanes); charged: worst path 929.
Checks (all after the counted region): 1 every counted lane against blst's exported API with the kernel's line
y' = mu (x' - x2) + y2 (lanes 0..624 cover {0, 1, p-1, p-2, random} for x1, y1, x2, y2; y2 = 0 replaced by 1);
3 64 genuine G1 pairs, (x', y') equal to blst's affine P + (-T); 4 x1 = x2 = 0 lanes biased to X >= 2p;
5 largest product operands (t = y1 + y2 = 2p - 2, inv = p - 1 on odd lanes, x2 = 0 so w = x' + p up to 2p - 1).
The ancestor harness's check 2 (lazy-operand products through blst's exported API) is not repeated: the operand bound the
kernel needs is now the K1 lemma (proof.md section 1), checked by nocarry_witness.py and by check 5 here.
Ancestor record: the 971 listing (sha ba448d6b...) measured 964.920 per lane in fd385c98 / 99e03e91; every K1/K2
edit lies on all 24 paths, and the mean here is 41.995 lower (the lane mix of this harness differs slightly).
A first run of this harness used the other line formula y' = mu (x' - x1) - y1 as reference; it agreed only on the
genuine pairs (where inv is the true inverse) and was corrected to the kernel's formula before the run above.
